Z||000003||1FST2M6||07-03-2000||01:54 PM||||well 1142 miles from my door to his i left my house at 3:30 and got to his door step at 11:00am  then hopped in te GT and drove from Sioux Falls at1pm and arrived in Billings with NO troubles at 12:30am...<P>I LOVE MY NEW GT! hopped in it and was pleased at how well the auto trany pulls! She runs SO smooth and I was tol by Jeff that the car needed "some front end work" much to my surprise its WAY less than i had antisipated!  <P>I took jeff for a slide around the block.. stoped to let him drive nd we even more surprised that HE DIDN"T STALL!<P>also got the chance to meet Brad "Fierogod" owner of 16 fieros! and was driving a nice 3.1 SE!  <P>I'll be sure to keep everyone here posted on the GTs progress as well as jeff since he lost his baby... <P>Thanks Jeff for trading such a great car and I hope you have a good time with your new SE.<P><BR>PS. When your driving it.. take it past 4 to shift! its not a 3.1... drive it like a smaller mator .. TACH IT UP!~||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||07-03-2000||02:58 PM||||I'm glad to hear you made your trip without any problems.  I told the GT to treat you nicely, and she did. That tranny in the GT is really solid.  It always shifted nice and crisp doesn't slip at all.  I REALLY like the clutch in the SE.  Super positive grip.  It's not nearly as annoying as I would have thought. The clutch petal was a little different, but Brad figured out that the rod on that clutch petal that connects to the master cylinder was upside down. The car handles awesome BTW! Anyhow, I've already started getting parts together for her new motor.  It's going to be a 2.8 bored and stroked to 3.1  Anyhow, nuff rambling for now.  I'm glad you're happy with the GT. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||07-03-2000||03:06 PM||||BTW, I tried to make the front end sound like it needed more work than it actually did so that you wouldn't be dissapointed.||||reg||1
Z||000006||86SE||07-03-2000||06:19 PM||||Did you get that GT up on the dyno yet 1FTS2M6? ||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||07-10-2000||09:04 AM||||I'M HOME!  my 10 day vacation/car swap is over...  I made it to Montana with NO problems. The car will be shipped from Billings on the 11th and will be here in Atl. on the 18th. it'll be on the dyno the 19th when i can get out of work to pick it up. I'll be sure to keep everyone informed with it's progress... Glad to see you like your new toy.. OH they couldn't find the title down here.. I got home and it's in my hand signed and will be overnighted today ... you'll have it in the morning.  a 3.1 will be sweet! it really does need more torque!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   say hey to Brad for me. <P>made it from Menahga, MN to Atl. in 17:41.  and only saw 1 fiero on the street between there and here.. and it was a 4cyl being loaded on a flatbed/wrecker in Bloomington-Normal. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||BlackGT||07-10-2000||12:29 PM||||Hey GT Bastard...or should I now say SE Bastard,<P>I spoke to Trav today and you`re right he is <BR>a great guy and really cool people...I`m glad<BR>the trade worked out well for both of you! When he first told me he was considering this<BR>trade I wished I had some cash to just buy it<BR>from him....I really liked the car!! Once you<BR>learn how to drive that beast and add the nitrous you WILL be able to embarass a lot of<BR>other cars on the road...in fact you should be able to do that now but just remember to<BR>TACH IT UP!! I`ve driven that monster and she likes to be road hard so stop trying to<BR>be easy with the clutch! It`s either ON or OFF! I have the same clutch in my Black 86 GT<BR>and it`s my daily driver to and from work (76 miles round trip) you`ll learn how not<BR>to shake the dashboard while in traffic but<BR>once you have open road ...let it snap! Have<BR>fun with it!! ||||reg||6
Z||000009||GT Bastard||07-10-2000||02:54 PM||||I'm actually liking the clutch pretty well.  It's incredibly easy to chirp the tires.  I've pondered the idea of putting a regular heavy duty clutch in when the motor comes out, but I think I'll stick with this one.  gotta go...||||reg||1
Z||000010||GT Bastard||07-10-2000||04:29 PM||||If that GT doesn't Dyno better than stock I'm going to be surprised and P*SSED OFF after having pulled the motor apart to port heads and manifolds!  Brad is really curious too...  Oh yeah, I didn't mean to sound like a wuss for not tachin' up the SE, but it does make a slight knock so I'm trying to be really easy on it.  It doesn't seem to be getting worse, so I'll just treat her good until my new motor is together. The only time it's really evident is over 3,000 or when it first starts. I'd expected to replace the motor with a 3.1 very soon anyhow, so it's not a problem.  In fact, I've got the block, rods, crank all ready.  Just need to order a set of 3.1 hypereutectic pistons from Summit tomorrow. BTW, what color is the GT going to be?  You said you had an appointment to repaint it, but are you going to use maroon/silver again? Keep me posted!  later,<P>Jeff||||reg||1
